  "lineage": "Zouglou Ivorian student-and-popular music emerging in 1990 at the University of Abidjan dormitories as a participatory call-and-response song-and-dance form expressing political commentary. The genre arose from the older bidakouro Bété percussion-and-vocal tradition adapted with French-language and Nouchi-slang lyrics. Performance grew from a-cappella dormitory-circle form into commercial studio recording from 1992 onward. Magic System's 1ère Gaou (1999) became the first international-crossover zouglou hit.",
